  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chuma Chilimnthaka Soya Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture, Soya, Groundnuts, Beans Beneficiaries: 250 Location: Bwanje, Ntcheu Chuma Chilimnthaka Smallholder Farmers&apos; Association is an association in Ntcheu with 158 women and 92 men member farmers. The association grows a variety of crops, but mostly legumes and maize. The purpose of the organisation is to produce crops and collectively sell the crops in order to develop farmer members and improve their livelihood. USADF funds will assist the group with training, capacity building, working capital, and business planning..</narrative>
  </description>
